# true-toto — Project Overview

## What This Project Is

`true-toto` is a faithful CLI replica of the GNU Core Utilities `true` command.
It exits immediately with status code `0` (success), ignores every argument
passed to it, and produces no output — except when invoked with `--help` or
`--version`.

## Binary Name

The compiled binary must always be named **`true-toto`**. Never rename it.
On Windows, MinGW may also emit `true-toto.exe`; that is the same program.

## Platforms

| Platform | Build environment | Notes |
|----------|-------------------|-------|
| **Linux** | `gcc`/`clang` + GNU Make | Full POSIX path |
| **Windows** | **MSYS2 UCRT64** (recommended) | Native Windows `.exe`; no POSIX signal concerns |
| **Git Bash** | Works if `/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin` is **before** Anaconda on `PATH` | Same binary as UCRT64; see `toolchain-structure.mdc` |

Binaries are **not portable** across OSes — build separately on Linux and on Windows.

## Scope — Keep It Minimal

Supporting behaviour:

- Built-in `--help` / `--h` and `--version` / `--v` (detected anywhere in
  `argv`; help wins if both appear)
- All other arguments (including `--foo`, `-`, arbitrary strings) are silently
  ignored

**Do not add**:

- Interactive or TUI modes
- stdin reading
- Any output on the normal (no-flag) execution path
- Logging or debug output in normal operation
- Single-dash `-h` / `-v` (only `--help`, `--h`, `--version`, and `--v` are
  special)
- Any feature that would break GNU `true` behavioural compatibility

## Behavioural Contract

| Invocation | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| `true-toto` | exits `0` immediately; no output |
| `true-toto any args here` | exits `0`; ignores all args; no output |
| `true-toto --version` / `true-toto --v` | prints `true-toto <version>\n`, exits `0` |
| `true-toto --help` / `true-toto --h` | prints usage on stdout, exits `0` |
| `true-toto --help --version` | `--help` wins; prints usage, exits `0` |
| `true-toto --version --help` | `--help` wins; prints usage, exits `0` |

## Exit Codes

| Code | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `0` | Always — normal exit, `--help`, `--version`, or any arguments |
| `1` | Write failure when printing `--help` or `--version` text |

